    "summary": "High‑energy show with a stellar Dark Star > Comes A Time and tight second set",
    "blurb": "The July ’72 Paramount Theater gig delivers a standout Dark Star → Comes A Time that crackles with Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s bass bombs. Highlights also include a gorgeous Greatest Story Ever Told, a moving Stella Blue, and a crisp China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider pairing. Overall the performance is high‑energy with solid playing throughout.",
    "review": "July 26, 1972 finds the Dead in Portland at the Paramount Theater firing on all cylinders. The first set rolls smoothly through a tight mix of folk‑rock and country numbers before launching into a bright China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that sets up an energetic vibe for the night. The second set truly shines, opening with The Promised Land and quickly building to a smoking Dark Star → Comes A Time where Jerry’s sweet, soaring tone intertwines with Keith’s jazzy piano, while Phil drops massive bass bombs that drive the jam forward. Afterward the band keeps the momentum high with a powerful Greatest Story Ever Told, a lyrical Stella Blue, and a joyous Not Fade Away medley that closes the night on an uplifting note. The soundboard capture is crisp and well‑balanced (aside from occasional glitches), making this one of the more vivid snapshots of the early‑’70s era.",
